Test a host name's addresses at once. resolveHostName() connected to one address after another
with a 3 second timeout each, so a stale or unreachable address (an AAAA record without an IPv6
path) cost 3 seconds per address and port before a working one was tried. probeAddresses() now
starts a non-blocking connect to the first 8 addresses together and takes the earliest in
getaddrinfo's order that accepts it: once one answers, an earlier address still trying gets 250 ms
more. The losing sockets are closed. A single address without TCP_PORT_FLAG_ALWAYS_TEST is still
taken untested, and the IPv4 fallback for a synthesized IPv6 address is unchanged. The Rust engine
probes the same way (net::probe). Applies after decode-queue-bound.patch.

